  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Border Control Through Information Sharing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project will support enhanced border capacities of the Republic of Kazakhstan to counter transnational organized crime including the smuggling of migrants, trafficking in persons and irregular migration through greater detection of fraudulent travel documents and identities as well as creating a network of information sharing, understanding emerging trends to enhance operational decisions and policy making. The proposal will contribute to IOM&#x2019;s steps towards enhancing border management services&apos; access to data and analysis, via the Document Examination Support Center (DESC), to better focus on travel document verification on specific cases. The Government of Kazakhstan joining DESC, the platform established in 2012 originally for Asian-Pacific countries, will allow Law enforcement agencies to establish access to the Asian Network for Document Examination that combines data on falsified documents and fraudulent identity from different countries to analyze trends in illicit travel. In practice, this will allow the National authorities of DESC-implementing countries to strengthen their risk analysis and interventions at points of entry.</narrative>
  </description>
